     1	# Capability inventory
     2	
     3	The inventory defines the minimum real operator model for each module. Commercial products are comparison points for jobs and information architecture, not implementation dependencies.
     4	
     5	The comparison tables are the product target, not an implementation claim.
     6	The live manifest is authoritative for what can be enabled today: it exposes a
     7	truthful subset with exact domain handlers and schemas. Unsupported target
     8	capabilities are omitted. A function with no canonical operator service is
     9	`unavailable` and exposes nothing; ContentFn is folded into CmsFn rather than
    10	duplicating its server. This deliberately leaves roadmap gaps visible instead
    11	of filling them with generic payload/execute façades.
    12	
    13	## Live implementation status
    14	
    15	The catalog contains 29 administration packages: 18 required selectable
    16	modules, 2 optional selectable modules, 2 real nested modules, 1 folded empty
    17	module, and 6 unavailable empty modules. Only required and optional modules are
    18	independently selectable. Nested modules mount under their owner, folded
    19	modules cannot be selected independently, and unavailable modules fail closed.
    20	
    21	| Module | Live availability | Real implemented subset |
    22	| --- | --- | --- |
    23	| AuthFn | Required selectable | Scoped users and sessions: list/get/delete users, list a user's sessions, and revoke a session through AuthFn storage and hooks. |
    24	| BillFn | Required selectable | Products, plans, prices, subscriptions, entitlements, usage, payments, and reconciliation; change/cancel subscriptions, refund payments, and reconcile the provider through the configured BillFn instance. |
    25	| BrowseFn | Required selectable | Environment-bound provider availability, aggregate metrics, rate-limit state, sanitized lifecycle logs, and aggregate cache state; confirmed clearing of metrics, logs, or cache through the BrowseFn facade. |
    26	| CiFn | Required selectable | Control-plane runs, materialized jobs, redacted logs, and retained artifacts; trigger/retry/cancel runs and issue audited signed artifact downloads. |
    27	| CmsFn | Required selectable | Environment-bound ContentFn datasets, schemas, documents, and revisions; create/upsert/query/patch/delete, publish/unpublish, and restore revisions. |
    28	| CompFn | Required selectable | Scoped frameworks, controls, checks, evidence, and reports; collect evidence and generate auditor reports through the CompFn API. |
    29	| DataFn | Required selectable | Schemas, resources, relations, indices, capabilities, records, and query execution; query, mutate, and transact through the configured DataFn executor. |
    30	| FileFn | Required selectable | Authorized files, versions, upload sessions, grants, share links, policies, and processing artifacts; upload lifecycle, deletion, grants, one-time share creation/revocation, and processing through FileFn services. |
    31	| FlowFn | Required selectable | Environment-owned queues, jobs, workers, dead letters, and event log; pause/resume, enqueue, run/close workers, and redrive/delete/clean dead letters through FlowFn APIs. |
    32	| MailFn | Required selectable | Project-scoped projects, inboxes, messages, threads, drafts, attachments, credentials, domains, webhooks, retention, quotas, and audit events; the implemented inbox, message, draft, domain, webhook, credential, and retention actions. |
    33	| MemoryFn | Required selectable | Environment-scoped memory search and ingestion through the configured MemoryFn pipeline and storage adapter. |
